t, which states that for any vectors \\(\\mathbf{u}\\), \\(\\mathbf{v}\\), and \\(\\mathbf{w}\\), and any scalars \\(m\\) and \\(n\\), we have \\(\\mathbf{u} \\times (m\\mathbf{v} + n\\mathbf{w}) = m(\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}) + n(\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{w})\\). Applying this property, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{c} \\times (3 \\mathbf{a} - 2 \\mathbf{b}) = 3 (\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{a}) - 2 (\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{b}).\n\\]\n\nWe are given \\(\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{c} = \\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 2 \\end{pmatrix}\\), so \\(\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{a} = -\\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 2 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -4 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}\\). We are also given \\(\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 18 \\end{pmatrix}\\). Substituting these into the expression, we get:\n\n\n</partial_draft>","role":"user"},{"content":"Continue from the interruption. Output only the continuation. Do not restart the solution.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"b4c73fa7a700a086975112efc4148248fcc26c3765244744988abed9f5a1d9f0"},"seconds":20.120362520217896,"seed":396339230524910996,"stop":"eos","text":"\\[\n3 (\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{a}) - 2 (\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{b}) = 3 \\begin{pmatrix} -4 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix} - 2 \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 18 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nNow, perform the scalar multiplication and vector addition/subtraction:\n\n\\[\n3 \\begin{pmatrix} -4 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -12 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -6 \\end{pmatrix},\n\\]\n\\[\n-2 \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 18 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ 14 \\\\ -36 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nAdding these two vectors together, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} -12 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -6 \\end{pmatrix} + \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ 14 \\\\ -36 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -14 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -42 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} -14 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -42 \\end{pm